Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(core): coverage reads the queue's done status and
 reports the preview outcome beside it (C8)

completeJob writes the status done for every finished job. coverageStatus
mapped a preview's outcome only when the status was completed, a word no
Core queue writer stores, so a finished preview reached the owner's
coverage view as a bare done: a withheld preview and one awaiting owner
review looked the same, against the design doc's promise to keep them
distinct.

status now passes the queue's own word through unchanged (queued, running,
done or failed), and a done preview's outcome (withheld or
needs_owner_review) is reported beside it as preview_outcome, null until
the job is done. The unit test's hand-written row used completed, the word
that hid the defect; it now carries done and checks both fields. The
planner fixture and the design doc use the queue's words too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
