+Checkpoints contain per-surface `(timestamp,id)`, next surface and scanned count. Persist them only together with accepted existing-queue work in an existing orchestration job's input/output; do not persist a proposed checkpoint before enqueue succeeds. A withheld preview is not successful published coverage. `coverageStatus` projects job outcomes/review/metrics for the owner and keeps withheld, pending, needs-owner-review and published outcomes distinct: `status` is the queue's own word as Core writes it (`queued`, `running`, `done` or `failed`; never `completed`), and a `done` preview's outcome (`withheld` or `needs_owner_review`) is reported beside it as `preview_outcome`.
 
 **All plans return `dispatchable:false`.** Stable IDs prevent duplicate queue records via the existing upsert, but a pure snapshot cannot enforce shared daily/backlog caps across independent dispatchers. Before automatic scheduling, the existing data plane needs one atomic budget reservation + enqueue + checkpoint transaction. Before multi-character publication it also needs item-wide uniqueness and source/persona-version comparison in the atomic publication boundary. Existing SQL only provides per-actor article uniqueness and job replay. No new SQL or security policy is introduced here.
 
